<title>USA: UAW in tentative pact with Rolls Royce unit.</title>
<headline>UAW in tentative pact with Rolls Royce unit.</headline>
<dateline>INDIANPOLIS, Ind. 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United Auto Workers said Monday it reached a tentative agreement with Allison Engine Co, a unit of Rolls Royce Plc, on a new contract covering about 2,000 UAW Local 933 members at the company's Indianapolis engine plant.</p>
<p>Details of the new agreement are being withheld pending a ratification meeting scheduled for next week in Indianpolis.</p>
<p>It is the first new contract for UAW-Allison workers since the company was purchased from General Motors Corp in 1994.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
